  "correct_answer": "847",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Complete combustion of ethene&nbsp;and methane mixture produces carbon dioxide.<br />Let, Volume of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> litre</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>Initial volume of carbon dioxide 0<br />Final&nbsp;volume of carbon dioxide&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>Initial volume of carbon dioxide is 0</p><p>Final&nbsp;volume of carbon dioxide&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Total volume of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>PV</mi><mi>RT</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>082</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>298</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>229</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mole</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>082</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>298</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>458</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mole</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Heat evolved using standard enthalpy of combustion&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>229</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>900</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>458</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1400</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>206</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>641</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>847</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi></math></p>"
  }
